 1/IMG_1515-scaled.jpeg?ver=1736366132
UID:NyUJNLYbgIQ6IArHEkwLk
SUMMARY:How to Start a Startup
DTSTAMP:20260801T102137Z
DTSTART:20260819T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:You have an idea…now what?  \nBefore you start looking for fund
	ing\, it’s important to ensure that your idea is both viable and valuable 
	— if it doesn’t have a sound model and a market willing to pay for it\, in
	vestors won’t be interested anyway. \nJoin us after the session\, hosted b
	y Heath Butler\, for a networking happy hour! \nTarget Audience: \n\nStart
	ups and Entrepreneurs: early-stage entrepreneurs\, entrepreneurs testing i
	deas for a pivot\nCommunity Members: people with an idea for a startup but
	 unsure what to do next\, small business owners\nCorporate Innovators: int
	rapreneurs\, decision-makers tasked with creating and leading sustainable 
	change\nAcademic Partners: students or faculty with an idea for a startup\
	n\nAbout the Speakers:\nHeath Butler\, Mercury Fund \nHeath focuses on B2B
	 SaaS and B2B2C Marketplace investments in future-of-work and fin-tech the
	mes. Heath also manages the organization’s venture studio and network plat
	form\, including corporate\, service provider\, and startup community rela
	tionships. \nPrior to joining Mercury\, Heath co-founded Gestalt Theory Ve
	nture Partners\, a venture studio and angel investing group. Prior to Gest
	alt\, Heath held leadership roles as a seasoned go-to-market and corporate
	 development executive at Insperity (NYSE: NSP)\, the nation’s leading HR 
	outsourcing services provider. Prior to Insperity\, Heath led business dev
	elopment for EnergyWorkspace.com\, founded a fin-tech startup\, and develo
	ped his foundational management skills at UPS. \nOutside of Mercury\, Heat
	h is an active angel investor and advocates for democratizing access to pr
	ivate equity opportunities for all investors. He is an active startup in t
	he Houston innovation community\, a mentor\, and a regular speaker/mentor 
	within The Ion. Heath enjoys traveling with family and likes to read\, gol
	f\, cycle\, and is an avid poker player. \n \n\nhttps://iondistrict.com/ev
	ent/how-to-start-a-startup-8/\n\nFrom Ion District
URL:https://iondistrict.com/event/how-to-start-a-startup-8/
LOCATION:Ion – Forum Stairs\, 4201 Main St.\, Houston\, TX\, 77002\, United
	 States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:ion-district
CATEGORIES:Ion District
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
